  "aiContextParagraph": "Political discourse in India has intensified as the Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) and Congress leader Rahul Gandhi engage in a series of exchanges regarding national governance and foreign policy. Tensions surfaced following Gandhi’s remarks characterizing India as a minor participant in global geopolitics and questioning the leadership of the Prime Minister. In response, BJP officials accused Gandhi of lacking understanding of international relations. Concurrently, the parties have diverged on economic issues, with BJP representatives highlighting India's GDP growth—an achievement recently noted by international figures—while Gandhi has targeted the ruling party’s performance on regional issues, specifically citing negligence in Manipur. Further debate has been prompted by Gandhi’s public statements on foreign affairs, his stance on international alliances, and a letter from a Hindu seer regarding a specific social media post, reflecting a broad range of political and social disagreements.",
